A||||7||Jeff Blowers||Door Lock Frozen||||5||
Z||000000||Jeff Blowers||10-27-2001||04:20 PM||||My driver's side door lock is frozen and I would like to replace it.  Does anyone know how to go about doing this?  It appears that you have to take it out from the outside as the glass is in the way.  If so, how do you get the outer skin off.  I have tried removing some of the Tork's but there must be something else required to remove this.<P>------------------<BR>88 2.8 Formula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/swiftlink/fiero_pictures_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Jeff Blowers||10-27-2001||04:25 PM||||trying to get a picture to show with the signature also with this post.<P>------------------<BR>88 2.8 Formula<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/swiftlink/fiero_pictures_2.htm"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||10-27-2001||04:48 PM||||Hey Jeff,<P>Pix still don't work, eh?  <P>BTW - the center area of the door has a clip that goes into the door frame.  You must move the skin fwd (if I remember right) as you pull outward - this assumes all hardware has been removed.  Getting it back on the clip is real &^$*(^$(&, but necessary.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-27-2001||06:21 PM||||The outer skin doesn't have to come off, but the inner panel does.  Just remove the linkage and pull the C clip.  Make sure to cuss loudly when you drop the damn thing in the bottom of your door.  Once you've spent a few minutes cussing all things living, find a pair of long tweezers (needle nose pliers or a small hand work too) and retrieve the C clip.  Pull the old lock cyl out and stick the new one in.  Try to work the C clip back around the new lock cyl.  Remember to cuss loudly again when you drop the frickin' thing one more time. Reattach the linkage and reinstall the door panel.  VOILA!  You can now lock your keys in the car again. <P>Best of luck.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mbramble||10-27-2001||07:12 PM||||As was stated above, you don't need to remove the outer skin to replace the door lock.  But, part of your question was how to do so.  <P>You need to remove all the torx head screws on the inside of the door that hold the front and back edges of the door in place.  You have to remove the mirror (from inside, 2 10mm nuts).  Remove the trim molding at the center of the door.  Lift up the door handle and you will see a small black plastic pop fastener that holds the end of the long molding in place.  Pry up very carefully with a flat screwriver.  No need to remove the small piece of molding behind the handle.  Under the molding are two two small 7mm hex head screws that also need to be removed.  Remove the plastic rivets in the bottom of the door. Just carefully yank on them with a pair of pliers (don't break the door skin, just the rivets!).  They will have to be replaced.  Once all these fasteners have been removed, pull the door skin back around the lock area and pull the little clip off the back of the lock cylinder that holds the lock rod in place and pull out the rod that runs from the handle down to open the door latch.  Then lift the skin straight up to clear the channel it is sitting in at the top.<P>Or, read Ogre's Cave notes about door service.  Link is at the top of this and every page.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||SLYGUY||10-27-2001||11:27 PM||||You did try some WD-40 or something similar first right?<P>Good Luck.<P>Sly||||reg||5
Z||000006||MooCow||10-27-2001||11:39 PM||||I had the same problem and I replaced mine.  Before replacing it make sure that the key goes all the way in.  Mine didnt and I never knowticed it unitl I took it out and then the key would turn it.  Somehow it moved back so the ket wouldnt go in only looked like it did.  Also try to use some graphit to loosen the lock up first.  If that does not work then hopefully you have small hands to get the new one in.<BR>Good luck<P> Thanks Ken||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||10-28-2001||12:36 PM||||At the moment I forget just how much about the lock is in my cave....<P>Tip I don't think is in there....<P>If it's not already on the new lock, Install the clip that holds the link rod BEFORE you put the lock in the door. Then you just have to snap the rod in place. (It's made to work that way...)<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
